.TH MILLERX 1 "2026-11-23" "millerX 0.7.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
millerx \- a small file browser with Miller columns
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B millerx
.RI [ FOLDER | FILE ]...
.br
.B millerx
.B \-\-version
.br
.B millerx
.B \-\-dbus
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B millerX
shows every folder from
.I /
down to where you are in its own column, and previews the selected file on the
right: pictures, a video's frame, a song's cover, the first page of PDFs, text and
the contents of archives. A folder's pictures show as thumbnails under its details.
.PP
Without arguments it opens your home folder. A
.I FOLDER
opens there; a
.I FILE
opens its folder with the file highlighted. Each argument gets its own window.
.PP
It needs no service running in the background. Optional programs add more
previews when they are installed:
.BR ffmpeg (1)
(video frames, music covers, AVIF and HEIC),
.BR pdftoppm (1)
(PDF pages),
.B blender\-thumbnailer
(pictures saved in Blender files) and
.BR pkexec (1)
(Open as root).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-dbus
Start without a window and wait up to 30 seconds for a "Show in folder" request
over D\-Bus (org.freedesktop.FileManager1), then open only the window asked for.
Meant for a D\-Bus service file, see
.BR FILES .
.SH KEYS
.TP 18
.BR "Left" ", " "Right"
previous / next column
.TP
.BR "Backspace" ", " "Alt+Up"
up one level
.TP
.BR "Alt+Home" ", " "Alt+/"
home folder, the Computer column (disks, USB sticks, network)
.TP
.B Enter
open
.TP
.B F2
rename
.TP
.BR "Delete" ", " "Shift+Delete"
move to the trash, delete permanently
.TP
.B Ctrl+C, Ctrl+X, Ctrl+V
copy, cut, paste (shared with Thunar's clipboard)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+N
new folder
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
search names in this folder and every folder below it; Escape goes back
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
bookmark this folder
.TP
.B Ctrl+H
show hidden files
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
location bar
.TP
.B Alt+Enter
properties
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
new window at this folder
.TP
.B Ctrl+,
settings
.TP
.B F5
reload
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q, Ctrl+W
close the window
.PP
Typing letters jumps to the first name starting with them; the same letter again goes
to the next one. Middle\-click a folder to open it in a new window. The trash is the
last line of the bookmarks menu.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/millerx/millerx.conf
settings (also changed from Menu \(-> Settings)
.TP
.I ~/.config/millerx/sorting.conf
folders sorted their own way, one per line
.TP
.I ~/.config/gtk\-3.0/bookmarks
bookmarks, shared with Thunar and the GTK file dialogs
.TP
.I ~/.config/mimeapps.list
default programs, written by Open with \(-> Set default
.TP
.I ~/.cache/thumbnails/
thumbnails, shared with Thunar; cleaned up automatically
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/dbus\-1/services/org.freedesktop.FileManager1.service
not made by millerX: create it with
.RS
.nf
[D\-BUS Service]
Name=org.freedesktop.FileManager1
Exec=/usr/bin/millerx \-\-dbus
.fi
.RE
to have millerX started for a browser's "Show in folder" when no file manager
is running.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERMINAL
the terminal for "Open terminal here" (may include arguments); otherwise the first
of 17 known terminals that is installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thunar (1),
.BR xdg\-mime (1)
.PP
https://github.com/overcatbe/millerx
.SH AUTHOR
overcatbe
